"epic comment pane" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-comment-pane&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-comment-pane&gt; element: the floating pane you write a new comment in.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>The small floating pane you write a NEW comment in:  a bullhorn's, or ⌘ / Ctrl I's on selected text.  It saves itself as you type;  once closed, the comment is a thread.  Paste or drop a picture in it (⌘ V, a screenshot too):  it is saved beside the page, and its path goes into your words, shown as a picture in the thread.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone changing how comments look or work on a page.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary (every name it uses): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-comment-pane-epiccommentpane-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-comment-pane/EpicCommentPane.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-comment-pane/EpicCommentPane.en.ts" code>EpicCommentPane.en.ts</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-comment-pane-epiccommentpane-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-comment-pane/EpicCommentPane.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-comment-pane/EpicCommentPane.tsx" code>EpicCommentPane.tsx</></>, with its style sheet (<text code>.css</>) and tests beside it.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>Click any bullhorn on this page (the masthead's, a section title's):  that's this element, opened by the comments' code under it.  It's fixed on the screen, so no copy of it sits here.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-comment-pane headline="“2. Context”" about="On a section in “2. Context”" saved="Saved 14:02 · waiting for Claude" deletable>
			  <textarea class="spell-comment-field" rows="3" aria-label="Your comment"></textarea>
			</epic-comment-pane>
			```
		</>
		<text paragraph>Its <text code>near</> property, <text code>&#123; left, top, bottom &#125;</>, is the box of what you clicked or selected.</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Name</>
				<cell>Values</>
				<cell>Meaning</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>headline</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>The first words it's on, in quotes, or <text code>This page</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>about</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>Which block it's on, in full:  its header's tooltip.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>saved</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>The floppy, and its tooltip.  It fades out 10 seconds after the save, or at once when something new is typed;  a red one stays.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>failed</>
				</>
				<cell>boolean</>
				<cell>The last save failed:  the floppy red.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>deletable</>
				</>
				<cell>boolean</>
				<cell>Saved:  the trash shows.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>near</>
				</>
				<cell>JSON (a property)</>
				<cell>Where to open:  8px under it, above it when there's no room below, inside the window.</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Events" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Event</>
					<cell>When</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>epic-comment-closing</>
					</>
					<cell>×:  the comments' code saves what's typed, then closes it.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>epic-comment-removing</>
					</>
					<cell>The trash:  deleted at once, Undo in the toast.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="4. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Ivory, 8px inside on every side, lifted off the page by a shadow;  no buttons below its text.</>
			<item>Its header:  the bullhorn, the first words (italic, cut short), the floppy, the trash, ×.  You drag it by its header.</>
			<item>The page never scrolls for it (2026-10-10:  "don't scroll the page and lose context!").</>
		</>
	</>
